From 10c6c6b1e23524fc8f2279b90aa5667c22907f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:11:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] Implement the Windows core: session, live API, danmaku,
 QR login

Replaces the stub's 35 {"event":"unsupported"} answers with the real thing,
ported from core/Sources/LiveHimeCore. The Qt UI shell is unchanged and was
already complete; this is the layer it was calling into.

  auth/session      the SessionState machine and its seven notices
  auth/qrlogin      generate/poll, the 1500 ms sleep-then-poll, three codes
  live/liveclient   nav, room fallback chain, areas, start/stop, title,
                    danmaku servers, emoticons, moderation
  live/danmaku      WinHTTP WebSocket, the 16-byte header, zlib bodies,
                    heartbeat, backoff, all thirteen room event kinds
  core/qr           qrcodegen (MIT) plus a zlib PNG writer for the login code

The foundation from the previous commit carries it: WinHTTP under net/, BCrypt
under net/crypto, the WBI and pc_link signers, and Credential Manager.

Deliberate deviations, each with the reason in the code: danmaku negotiates
protover 2 because brotli is in neither Windows nor obs-deps (version 3 is a
named failure, never a silent drop); the WebSocket read accumulates across
fragments where URLSession handed over whole messages; the credential store
falls back to a DPAPI file above Credential Manager's 2560-byte cap.

A self-test runs with LIVEHIME_SELFTEST=1 and writes what it observed to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\LiveHime\selftest.txt, because a Windows core otherwise has no
way to prove its network stack without a human driving the dock. Verified in
the VM against the real Bilibili: nav answers 200/-101 with the WBI keys
present, qrcode/generate answers 200/0 with a scannable URL, and driving
StartQrLogin() puts a rendered QR code in the dock.

Known, and not hidden: the dock's QR page is wider than the 404 px the dock is
given on Windows, so the code is clipped; brotli, WebView2 (web login, cover,
face auth), captions and the update checker are still pending.

