+ * BilibiliLiveClient.swift, LiveRoomActions.swift, BilibiliControlClient.swift
+ * and the Emoticons half of Emoticons.swift.
+ *
+ * The rule for this port (CONTRACT) is to behave like the Swift, not like a
+ * reasonable person's idea of what the Swift meant. Where the Swift is odd —
+ * the eight-field startLive signature, the room-lookup fallback chain, reading
+ * the WBI keys out of a -101 nav answer without the usual code check — the C++
+ * does the same thing and the comment cites the file:line it came from.
+ *
+ * Every public callback leaves through dispatch::Post, so it runs on the main
+ * thread exactly once, including when the transport failed. Errors are shaped
+ * per CONTRACT §4.3 and only sessionExpired sets `logged_out` (CONTRACT §4.1).
+ * The stream key is a secret: it travels in Result<StreamConfig> and nowhere
+ * else — this file never logs or emits.
+ *
+ * Not ported from the Swift, each called out where it would have run:
+ * BilibiliDiagnosticStore (the C++ probe entry point is a later milestone) and
+ * the ImageIO re-encode plus the cache-trim task of Emoticons.swift. */
